:PNLGRP.
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für den Befehl
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP NAME='PEEK'.
File Editor - Peek/400 (PEEK) - Help
:P.
Peek/400 is a file editor used to display, create, change and
delete records of a given database file and member.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort FILE
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='PEEK/FILE'.
Datei - Help
:XH3.File (FILE)
:P.
Specifies the name and library of the database file
containing the records to be displayed.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/REQPARM'.
:P.
:HP2.Qualifier 1: File:EHP2.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.Name:EPV.
:PD.Name of the physical or logical file containing the records.
:EPARML.
:P.
:HP2.Qualifier 2: Library:EHP2.
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.All libraries of the current job are searched until the
file is found.
:PT.:PV.*CURLIB:EPV.
:PD.The current library of the job is used to locate the
file. If no library is specified as the current library
for the job, the QGPL library is used.
:PT.:PV.Name:EPV.
:PD.Name of the library to be searched.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort MEMBER
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='PEEK/MEMBER'.
Member - Help
:XH3.Member (MEMBER)
:P.
Specifies the name of the file member containing the records.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The records of the first member of the specified file
are displayed.
:PT.:PV.*NONE:EPV.
:PD.No member is opened. This special value can be used for
displaying external data structures.
:PT.:PV.Name:EPV.
:PD.Name of the member containing the records to be displayed.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort ACCESS
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='PEEK/ACCESS'.
Type of record access - Help
:XH3.Type of record access (ACCESS)
:P.
Specifies the sort sequence and the how to select the records
that are displayed.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*KEY:EPK.
:PD.All records of the specified file are displayed
in key sequence. If the file does not have a key the
records are shown by record number.
:PT.:PV.*RRN:EPV.
:PD.All records of the specified file are displayed
by record number.
:PT.:PV.*SQL:EPV.
:PD.All records matching the criteria specified at parameter
:HP2.SQL WHERE (WHERE):EHP2. are selected and displayed according
to the sort sequence given at parameter :HP2.SQL ORDER BY
(ORDERBY):EHP2..
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort LANGUAGE
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='PEEK/LANGUAGE'.
Language - Help
:XH3.Language (LANGUAGE)
:P.
Specifies the language of the Peek/400 user interface and
messages. The name of the message file consists of
'PEEK' plus a 3-digit language identifier, such as GER (German),
ENG (English), ITA (Italian) or SPA (Spanish).
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The language of the user settings is used. If Peek/400 is
started for the first time, the language is retrieved from
key *LANGUAGE in file PEEKUSR.
:PT.:PV.Language:EPV.
:PD.Specifies the 3-digit language identifier that is used
to identify the message file containing the language constants.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort ALWCHGLIB
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='PEEK/ALWCHGLIB'.
Allow to change library - Help
:XH3.Allow to change library (ALWCHGLIB)
:P.
Specifies whether or not it is allowed to change the name of
the library that contains the file whose records are displayed.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The actual value is provided by EXIT programm EXIT01.
:PT.:PV.*YES:EPV.
:PD.The library can be changed at any time.
:PT.:PV.*NO:EPV.
:PD.The library cannot be changed from the main screen of
Peek/400.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort ALWCHGFILE
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='PEEK/ALWCHGFILE'.
Allow to change file - Help
:XH3.Allow to change file (ALWCHGFILE)
:P.
Specifies whether or not it is allowed to change the name of
the file containing the records to be displayed.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The actual value is provided by EXIT programm EXIT01.
:PT.:PV.*YES:EPV.
:PD.The file can be changed at any time.
:PT.:PV.*NO:EPV.
:PD.The file cannot be changed from the main screen of
Peek/400.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort ALWCHGMBR
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='PEEK/ALWCHGMBR'.
Allow to change member - Help
:XH3.Allow to change member (ALWCHGMBR)
:P.
Specifies whether or not it is allowed to change the name of
the member containing the records to be displayed.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The actual value is provided by EXIT programm EXIT01.
:PT.:PV.*YES:EPV.
:PD.The member can be changed at any time.
:PT.:PV.*NO:EPV.
:PD.The member cannot be changed from the main screen of
Peek/400.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort ALWCHGRCD
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='PEEK/ALWCHGRCD'.
Allow to change records - Help
:XH3.Allow to change records (ALWCHGRCD)
:P.
Specifies whether or not it is allowed to add, change,
delete or copy records.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The actual value is provided by EXIT programm EXIT01.
:PT.:PV.*YES:EPV.
:PD.records can be added, chnaged, deleted or copied
at any time.
:PT.:PV.*NOKEY:EPV.
:PD.Key fields are locked and cannot be modified.
:PT.:PV.*NO:EPV.
:PD.Records cannot be added, changed, deleted or copied.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort ALWCHGSQLW
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='PEEK/ALWCHGSQLW'.
Allow to change SQL WHERE - Help
:XH3.Allow to change SQL WHERE (ALWCHGSQLW)
:P.
Specifies whether or not it is allowed to change the
SQL WHERE clause used to select the records to be displayed.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The actual value is provided by EXIT programm EXIT01.
:PT.:PV.*YES:EPV.
:PD.The SQL WHERE clause can be changed at any time.
:PT.:PV.*NO:EPV.
:PD.The SQL WHERE clause is locked and cannot be changed.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort ALWCHGSQLO
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='PEEK/ALWCHGSQLO'.
Allow to change SQL ORDER BY - Help
:XH3.Allow to change SQL ORDER BY (ALWCHGSQLO)
:P.
Specifies whether or not it is allowed to change the
SQL ORDER BY clause that defines the sort sequence of
the records.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The actual value is provided by EXIT programm EXIT01.
:PT.:PV.*YES:EPV.
:PD.The SQL ORDER BY clause can be changed at any time.
:PT.:PV.*NO:EPV.
:PD.The SQL ORDER BY clause is locked and cannot be changed.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort ENVFILE
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='PEEK/ENVFILE'.
Environment - Help
:XH3.Environment (ENVFILE)
:P.
Specifies the name and library of the file that is used
to save the settings of a Peek/400 workspace.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
:P.
:HP2.Qualifier 1: File:EHP2.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.Name:EPV.
:PD.Name of the file to save a Peek/400 workspace.
:EPARML.
:P.
:HP2.Qualifier 2: Library:EHP2.
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.All libraries of the current job are searched until the
file is found.
:PT.:PV.Name:EPV.
:PD.Name of the library that contains the file used to save
a Peek/400 workspace.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort ENVMBR
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='PEEK/ENVMBR'.
Member - Help
:XH3.Member (ENVMBR)
:P.
Specifies the name of the member used to load the Peek/400
workspace settings.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The name of the member that contains the records displayed is
the same as the name of the member that used to load the Peek/400
workspace settings.
:PT.:PV.*FIRST:EPV.
:PD.The workspace settings are loaded from the first member.
:PT.:PV.Name:EPV.
:PD.The workspace settings are loaded from the specified member.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort ENVSAVE
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='PEEK/ENVSAVE'.
Save on Exit - Help
:XH3.Save on Exit (ENVSAVE)
:P.
Specifies whether or not the current environment is saved
to the specified environment file and member when the program
ends.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The current environment settings are not automatically saved
to the specified environemnt file and member.
:PT.:PV.*YES:EPV.
:PD.The current environment settings are automatically saved to
the specified environment file and member.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort ENVLAYOUT
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='PEEK/ENVLAYOUT'.
Load layout only - Help
:XH3.Load layout only (ENVLAYOUT)
:P.
Specifies whether or not to load only the layout from the
specified environment file and keep the specified file
and member.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The current environment settings are completely applied and
the specified member is overridden by the member of the
environment.
:PT.:PV.*YES:EPV.
:PD.Only the layout is loaded from the environment file. The
specified file and member are kept untouched and opended.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort SETTINGS
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='PEEK/SETTINGS'.
User settings - Help
:XH3.User settings (SETTINGS)
:P.
Specifies which user settings are used. By default the user settings
are stored in the Peek/400 product library. The name of the settings
file is equal to the name of the user profile that is signed on to
the system.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
:P.
:HP2.Element 1: File:EHP2.
:P.
:HP2.Qualifier 1: File:EHP2.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The name of the current user profile is used to identify
the user settings file.
:PT.:PV.Name:EPV.
:PD.Name of the file that contains the user settings.
:EPARML.
:P.
:HP2.Qualifier 2: Library:EHP2.
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRDLIB:EPK.
:PD.Specifies that the user settings file is stored in the
Peek/400 product library.
:PT.:PV.*LIBL:EPV.
:PD.All libraries of the current job are searched until the
file is found.
:PT.:PV.*CURLIB:EPV.
:PD.The current library of the job is used to locate the user
settings file. If no library is specified as the current library
for the job, the QGPL library is used.
:PT.:PV.Name:EPV.
:PD.Name of the library that contains the user settings file.
:EPARML.
:P.
:HP2.Element 2: User profile:EHP2.
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The name of the current user is used to load the user settings.
:PT.:PV.Name:EPV.
:PD.Name of the user profile used to load the user settings.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort WHERE
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='PEEK/WHERE'.
SQL WHERE - Help
:XH3.SQL WHERE (WHERE)
:P.
Specifies a SQL WHERE clause to select the records that are
displayed.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.All records are displayed.
:PT.:PV.Auswahlkriterien:EPV.
:PD.Only records matching the SQL WHERE clause are displayed.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort ORDERBY
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='PEEK/ORDERBY'.
SQL ORDER BY - Help
:XH3.SQL ORDER BY (ORDERBY)
:P.
Specifies a SQL ORDER BY clause to set the sort sequence
of the records that are displayed.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The selected records are displayed by record number.
:PT.:PK DEF.*KEY:EPK.
:PD.The selected records are displayed in key sequence. If
the file does not have a key the records are shown by record
number.
:PT.:PV.Sort sequence:EPV.
:PD.The selected records are displayed using the specified
sort sequence.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*====================================================================
.*  Textbausteine, die an mehreren Stellen im Hilfetext
.*  verwendet werden.
.*====================================================================

.*=====================================
.*  Erforderlicher Parameter
.*=====================================
:HELP NAME='COM/REQPARM'.
:P.
This is a required parameter.
:P.
:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.
:EHELP.

.*=====================================
.*  Optionaler Parameter
.*=====================================
:HELP NAME='COM/OPTPARM'.
:P.
This is an optional parameter.
:P.
:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.
:EHELP.

.*=====================================
.*  Werteliste
.*=====================================
:HELP NAME='COM/VALUES'.
:P.
The possible values are:
:EHELP.
.*
:EPNLGRP.
